ext iteration check that (1) composite selection is no longer overwhelmed by extreme design_cost values, (2) auxiliary objectives continue improving, and (3) reported design_cost values are inspected for normalization (should be in [0,1]). If design_cost outputs are still invalid, follow-up action should be to either sanitize the scorer outputs or drop the objective.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.7, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "Reasoning: The analyzer shows a clear mismatch between the documented design_cost range [0,1] and observed values (mean = -7.0604e10, std = 7.8026e9, best = -7.2005e10). This indicates the design_cost scorer is mis-scaled or sign-inverted and is likely dominating selection. A quick, low-risk mitigation is to reduce the effective weight of design_cost so the working auxiliary objectives can guide exploration until the scorer is fixed.\n\n<decision>{\n  \"failure_location\": \"implementation\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The 'design_cost' scorer is mis-scaled or sign-inverted (returns large negative values instead of [0,1]), causing it to dominate selection; I am moderately confident but not certain.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"objective\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Observed design_cost mean = -7.0604e10 (expected in [0,1]) \u2014 orders of magnitude off. parameter_spread and parameter_mean are moving in desired directions. Temporarily reducing design_cost weight (minimum allowed) will prevent the broken scorer from overwhelming selection while preserving some influence until the scorer is corrected.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"ops\": [\n      {\n        \"op\": \"set_weight\",\n        \"name\": \"design_cost\",\n        \"weight\": 0.05\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Prevents the mis-scaled design_cost from dominating multi-objective aggregation, allowing parameter_spread and parameter_mean (weights 0.3 and 0.2) to steer exploration. Retains minimal influence from design_cost so that when it is repaired its signal is not entirely lost.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"In the next iteration check that (1) composite selection is no longer overwhelmed by extreme design_cost values, (2) auxiliary objectives continue improving, and (3) reported design_cost values are inspected for normalization (should be in [0,1]). If design_cost outputs are still invalid, follow-up action should be to either sanitize the scorer outputs or drop the objective.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.7\n}</decision>", "change_id": "d8ff06e2acf74e95", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [{"op": "set_weight", "name": "design_cost", "weight": 0.05}], "implementation_patches": {}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [2000, 2001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["design_cost", "parameter_spread", "parameter_mean"], "baseline_objectives": ["design_cost", "parameter_spread", "parameter_mean"], "baseline": [2.4479597608038354e-06, 1.1498802238231458e-05], "candidate": [1.7506674310458055e-07, 3.4777626824540155e-08], "baseline_mean": 6.973380999517647e-06, "candidate_mean": 1.0492218496456035e-07, "delta": -6.8684588145530865e-06, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 2.0548499396809805e-05, "population_mean": 7.178316247117581e-06, "best": 3.338882557751529e-05, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 7.829033265704778e-05, "population_mean": 2.3175049943062887e-05, "best": 0.00010723690673833124, "n_invalid": 0}], "candidate": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 1.4846311640737754e-06, "population_mean": 4.951023902778662e-07, "best": 3.3266586749888666e-06, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 6.931877497864095e-07, "population_mean": 1.1617243992680343e-07, "best": 1.8983030602788938e-06, "n