{"schema_version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T15:48:14.522743", "run_id": "ab-real_llm-underflow_cost-s1-B-20261020154559", "task_id": "underflow_cost", "seed": 1, "iteration": 2, "mode": "meta_controller_on", "judge": {"judge_type": "llm", "model_name": "openai/gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "call_args": {}, "max_parse_retries": 1, "prompt_version": "v1"}, "validator": {"name": "underflow_cost_truth", "higher_is_better": true, "top_k": 5, "ranking": "population order (system ranking)", "draws": {"validation": 48, "test": 256, "calibration": 64}, "synthetic": true}, "acceptance_rule": {"split": "validation", "seeds": [2000, 2001], "min_improvement": 0.02, "rule": "accept iff all trials ran, no constraint violation, budget not exceeded, and mean(candidate) - mean(baseline) > 0 and >= min_improvement"}, "accepted_state_version_before": 0, "decision": {"failure_location": "implementation", "root_cause_hypothesis": "The registered 'design_cost' scorer appears to be returning unnormalized/incorrect (large negative) values (mean -7.130e10 \u00b1 3.9106e9) instead of the documented [0,1] range, causing it to dominate or corrupt multi-objective aggregation.", "intervention_target": "objective", "rationale": "Analyzer evidence: design_cost population mean = -7.130e10 \u00b1 3.9106e9 (best -7.2005e10), expected range [0,1]. Meanwhile parameter_spread = 0.4427 \u00b1 0.0182 (improving) and parameter_mean = 0.3707 \u00b1 0.0171 (worsening). Because design_cost outputs are numerically invalid, they likely distort selection. Dropping design_cost temporarily lets the optimizer rely on the two consistent scorers (parameter_spread, parameter_mean) until the scorer is fixed.", "proposed_change": {"ops": [{"op": "drop", "name": "design_cost"}]}, "expected_benefit_hypothesis": "Immediate removal of a corrupted objective that produces extreme-magnitude scores, preventing it from skewing candidate ranking. Subsequent iterations will use only parameter_spread and parameter_mean (weights 0.6/0.4), yielding reliable, interpretable progress and allowing focused debugging/fixing of design_cost without wasting optimization budget.", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "Run the next iteration(s) with design_cost removed and verify (1) the objective set no longer contains 'design_cost', (2) no huge-magnitude scores appear in reports, and (3) the optimizer's reported selection metrics are driven by parameter_spread and parameter_mean (population stats remain in expected ranges: spread ~[0,0.5], mean ~[0,1]). The independent validator should confirm an improvement relative to the previous accepted state by demonstrating removal of the corrupted scorer's influence on selection.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.75, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "Analyzer shows a critical scorer inconsistency: design_cost reported mean = -7.130e10 \u00b1 3.9106e9 (best -7.2005e10), which contradicts the documented [0,1] range and can catastrophically dominate multi-objective ranking. The most rapid, low-risk mitigation is to remove the corrupted objective from the active objective set until the scorer is fixed, so selection is driven by the two numerically-sensible parameter objectives.\n\n<decision>{\n  \"failure_location\": \"implementation\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The registered 'design_cost' scorer appears to be returning unnormalized/incorrect (large negative) values (mean -7.130e10 \u00b1 3.9106e9) instead of the documented [0,1] range, causing it to dominate or corrupt multi-objective aggregation.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"objective\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Analyzer evidence: design_cost population mean = -7.130e10 \u00b1 3.9106e9 (best -7.2005e10), expected range [0,1]. Meanwhile parameter_spread = 0.4427 \u00b1 0.0182 (improving) and parameter_mean = 0.3707 \u00b1 0.0171 (worsening). Because design_cost outputs are numerically invalid, they likely distort selection. Dropping design_cost temporarily lets the optimizer rely on the two consistent scorers (parameter_spread, parameter_mean) until the scorer is fixed.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"ops\": [\n      {\n        \"op\": \"drop\",\n        \"name\": \"design_cost\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Immediate removal of a corrupted objective that produces extreme-magnitude scores, preventing it from skewing candidate ranking. Subsequent iterations will use only parameter_spread and parameter_mean (weights 0.6/0.4), yielding reliable, interpretable progress and allowing focused debugging/fixing of design_cost without wasting optimization budget.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Run the next iteration(s) with design_cost removed and verify (1) the objective set no longer contains 'design_cost', (2) no huge-magnitude scores appear in reports, and (3) the optimizer's reported selection metrics are driven by parameter_spread and parameter_mean (population stats remain in expected ranges: spread ~[0,0.5], mean ~[0,1]). The independent validator should confirm an improvement relative to the previous accepted state by demonstrating removal of the corrupted scorer's influence on selection.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.75\n}</decision>", "change_id": "2e0b40b06648456a", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [{"op": "drop", "name": "design_cost"}], "implementation_patches": {}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [2000, 2001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["parameter_spread", "parameter_mean"], "baseline_objectives": ["design_cost", "parameter_spread", "parameter_mean"], "baseline": [5.574867178799229e-07, 4.855374406060605e-07], "candidate": [1.5315581854445724e-07, 1.4820904445155692e-07], "baseline_mean": 5.215120792429916e-07, "candidate_mean": 1.506824314980071e-07, "delta": -3.708296477449845e-07, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split